\title{communityhierarchy: Joint Inference of Communities and Hierarchy in Directed Networks}
\description{
Fits a joint Bayesian model of community structure and ranking in directed networks of wins, losses and draws, and measures how much of the ranking the communities explain. The undirected network follows a degree-corrected stochastic block model (Peixoto 2017 \doi{10.1103/PhysRevE.95.012317}), each interaction is decided by the Bradley-Terry model, with draws as in Davidson (1970) \doi{10.1080/01621459.1970.10481082}, and a node's score is its group's score plus an individual deviation. The posterior is sampled by Markov chain Monte Carlo with merge-split moves (Peixoto 2020 \doi{10.1103/PhysRevE.102.012305}) in a C++ core shared with the 'Python' package 'community-hierarchy'.
}
